interface.longDescription:
emoji.dance is a website where people DJ songs to each other in shared rooms: everyone in a room hears the same song at the same time while their emoji avatars dance and they chat. When it's your turn to DJ, you play from your selected playlist.

With emoji.dance connected, ChatGPT can make those playlists for you. Ask for a playlist by mood, genre, decade or artist, and ChatGPT finds each song on YouTube, SoundCloud, Vimeo or Dailymotion and saves it to your emoji.dance account. It can also:
- show your playlists and the songs in them;
- add songs to a playlist, at the bottom or the top (what you play next);
- take songs off a playlist;
- choose which playlist you DJ from;
- show the popular rooms right now, or look up a room by its link.

Changes show at once in any emoji.dance tab you have open.

You need an emoji.dance account (log in with Google when you connect). The app can't chat, join a room, play music, delete playlists, see your email or payments, or see anyone else's playlists. A playlist holds up to 100 songs, and an account keeps a limited number of playlists. Some videos can't be played outside their own site; those are marked unplayable in the room.
